1","time_limit":25},{"id":"pt_batch9_conditional_variance_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $X$ takes $1$ and $3$ equally likely within $B$, what is $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B)$?","options":["$2$","$0$","$1$","$4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8fc32fb181f8d8c78583cbc5","time_limit":25},{"id":"pt_batch9_conditional_variance_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why can conditioning reduce variance?","options":["Conditioning always shrinks the variance, whatever the event","Information may restrict the possible values of $X$","Conditioning lowers the mean, and variance falls with the mean","Information makes $X$ independent of the conditioning event"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b7f3794bf5fcad80c9b1267c","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch9_conditional_variance_009_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $\\mathbb{E}[X^2]<\\infty$, let $B_1,\\dots,B_n$ partition the sample space with $p_i=\\mathbb{P}(B_i)>0$, and let $Q=\\sum_i p_i\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B_i)$. Which statement holds for every such $X$ and partition?","options":["$Q=\\operatorname{Var}(X)$","$Q\\ge\\operatorname{Var}(X)$","$\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B_i)\\le\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ for every $i$","$Q\\le\\operatorname{Var}(X)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f659ed85e1f5c455e07c1448","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch9_conditional_variance_020_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"$X$ takes the values $0,1,2$ with probabilities $\\tfrac{1}{2},\\tfrac{1}{4},\\tfrac{1}{4}$, and $B=\\{X\\ge1\\}$. What is $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B)$?","options":["$\\tfrac{13}{16}$","$\\tfrac{1}{4}$","$\\tfrac{11}{16}$","$\\tfrac{5}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8a4208a9234629462aae350c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_probability_theory_for_eor_conditional_variance_99953059_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"A random variable $X$ with finite variance and an event $B$ with $\\mathbb{P}(B)=\\frac{1}{2}$ satisfy $\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid B]=0$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B)=1$, $\\mathbb{E}[X\\mid B^c]=4$ and $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid B^c)=5$. What is $\\operatorname{Var}(X)$?","options":["$3$","$11$","$4$","$7$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4024f4266ff4d0e55ef1e55d","time_limit":40}]}}